AB  - Connected vehicle platform is a software infrastructure that enables remote monitoring and control of vehicle software over networks, providing various value-added services to car owners. The platform connects a large number of vehicles simultaneously, and therefore, a system failure has a significant impact on users. Accurate fault detection and rapid recovery planning are imperative for providing a highly available connected vehicle system. To address this challenge, this paper introduces a multi-agent approach to automate fault localization and program repair on a connected vehicle platform. Given the distributed nature of the system, our LLM-based agent collects system configuration information, application code, and server logs to localize the root cause of system errors. Subsequently, a repair planning agent generates actionable recovery plans, consisting of necessary program repairs and system configuration updates. We implemented a prototype of the proposed system using the OpenAI Agents SDK and evaluated the effectiveness through a concrete failure case study. Compared to a single-agent system, our multi-agent-based system can generate a more rigorous recovery plan that includes code-level repair suggestions in addition to server-level configuration updates.
