AB  - Predicting stock portfolio crashes in Vietnam is challenging due to dynamic financial news. Large language models (LLMs) offer promise via zero-shot reasoning. This study introduces Temporal Personalized Relational Reasoning (TPRR), an enhanced framework building on Temporal Relational Reasoning (TRR), to model human-like cognitive processes for crash detection. TPRR integrates the Temporal Personalized PageRank (TPP) algorithm for improved graph weighting through temporal decay and personalized prioritization. We also propose a hybrid architecture combining deep learning for entity extraction and sentiment analysis with LLMs for relationship expansion, optimizing efficiency and robustness. Experiments on Vietnamese financial news (Jan 1- Apr 7, 2025) show that TPRR with deep learning achieves an AUROC of 0.781, outperforming baseline TRR (0.738). This work underscores TPRR's potential for complex financial forecasting tasks in Vietnam.
