AB  - The Philippines, highly vulnerable to natural disasters, often experiences communication outages that hinder emergency response efforts. This study introduces a satellite-based Automatic Packet Reporting System (APRS) payload designed to provide alternative communication during disasters. Operating in Digipeater Mode for real-time message retransmission and Store-and-Forward Mode for collecting and relaying environmental data from Ground Sensor Terminals (GSTs), the payload enhances situational awareness and supports rapid decision-making. Built with Commercial Off-The-Shelf (COTS) components with proven spaceflight heritage, the modular design underwent iterative testing to ensure reliability, energy efficiency, and seamless integration with CubeSat platforms. Beyond emergency communication, the system facilitates remote sensing applications, such as environmental monitoring and precision agriculture, by enabling data collection from remote areas. Future work will focus on enhancing RF shielding, conducting environmental testing, and expanding its functionality for disaster resilience and sustainable development, positioning the APRS payload as a critical tool for disaster-prone regions.
